vcore-netstack
Copyright 2026 VCore contributors

This crate was independently adapted for VCore after studying the
`clash-netstack` crate in clash-rs:

    https://github.com/Watfaq/clash-rs/tree/master/clash-netstack

The studied crate declares `MIT OR Apache-2.0`. This derivative crate is
distributed under Apache-2.0.

Material VCore changes include:

* replaced every unbounded channel with bounded channels or a coalescing
  `Notify` wake-up;
* replaced the unsafe lock-free application ring with a safe, capacity-limited
  byte queue;
* changed the default per-socket buffers from 256 KiB at each layer to a total
  configurable 32 KiB budget per direction;
* combined packet and socket polling in one cancellable driver task;
* added explicit packet, accept and UDP queue limits while allowing active and
  half-open TCP flow counts to follow workload;
* added a stop completion barrier and resource counters;
* kept UDP datagram boundaries and implemented IPv4 and IPv6 packet creation;
* added synthetic dual-stack, backpressure, stop and boundary tests.
